"""
distress_analysis.py

Builds a one-page high-yield distress dashboard from two ICE BofA H0A0
(US High Yield index) source files:

    Defaulted.xlsx  — bonds removed from the index due to default
    Index.xlsx      — current index composition

Produces a single Excel workbook (default: distress_analysis_output.xlsx) with
three sheets:

    Overview        — six formatted tables + bar charts, all on one sheet:
                        1. Top Defaulted Issuers (last 12 months, with sector)
                        2. Issuer Distress Ranking (current index)
                        3. Sector Exposure & Distress Concentration (rating-based)
                        4. Sector Distress by Spread — OAS > 1,000bps
                        5. Historical Defaults by Sector (full history)
                        6. Maturity Wall — CCC-and-Below vs. Full Index
    Index Snapshot  — current index composition on its own terms: summary
                        stats, rating-bucket distribution, sector exposure by
                        size, top 5 issuers, subordination-type breakdown.
    Methodology     — plain-language explanation of every filter, grouping,
                        and formula used in the workbook.

Usage:
    python distress_analysis.py --defaulted Defaulted.xlsx --index Index.xlsx
"""

